[Music]  when I was thinking about what exactly a  sequel to doom 2016 needed I thought of  the obvious more demons more guns and  cool new environments what I didn't  think about was mobility which in  retrospect was an obvious direction to  go in it doesn't get brought up much  when talking about it but doom 2016 had  a lot of platforming in it it was  primarily used to break up the pacing  and give a breather from combat  eventually it would become part of the  combat as well feeding into the game's  design of always needing to be on the  move in order to stay alive rather than  simply taking cover  but people praised doom for its combats  bloody visuals and head-banging  soundtrack not the platforming it got  the job done but it didn't feel  invigorating the way the rest of the  game did but doom eternal looks to fix  all that by making platforming and  mobility a core part of the experience I  think we wanted to make sure that the  incidental combat areas which is the  spaces in between the large combat  arenas would would be more interesting  you start to take those abilities and  combine them together what you get is  what we call traversal combos and and  you're gonna be able to do some really  cool things you can cover a lot of  ground with the monkey bar swing and  double jumping in two dashes and a  grapple hook and then you had wall climb  into that and I think it's gonna make  for some really interesting traversals  and it has an impact on the way the  levels are designed they're designed  maybe not so two-dimensional and flat  now we could do a lot more different  things that we couldn't do before we've  provided ourselves with the tools to be  able to make some really compelling  spaces simple additions like climbing  and air dashes open up the potential for  more interesting exploration and could  greatly improve the creativity required  to locate hidden secrets but the most  meaningful addition is what the game  refers to as the meathook a grappling  hook attached to the super shotgun that  pulls you towards demons this feeds  perfectly into dooms combat which is all  about killing demons as fast as possible  and that meathook is a great way to get  those deep  and your bullets to meet each other but  also has the potential to drastically  change the dynamics of combat and open  up new styles of play with aerial combos  it feels good to try to stay in the air  as long as you can and we give you a  bunch of these things to allow you to do  that absolutely that's the mini game it  happens it's just intuitive like you  feel like you want to do it so we  provide you with the chance to do it in  that yeah in fact in that second that  second kind of gameplay video that we  said we were gonna kind of make go you  know faster is keyboard and mouse non  cast off that player he's one of our  better players in the office Sean place  so so well because you can only you can  only grab but you can only meathook to  demons it's not a like a world grapple  like you can't grapple onto the side of  the building so you have to grapple to a  demon so he leaves a demon kind of  flying around so that he can use it as a  grapple point to get kind of wherever he  wants in the in this space so yeah I  mean it creates just more opportunities  more things to think about as you're as  you're playing the game more more  opportunities to kind of improv your way  through through the through the fight  choreography what we saw QuakeCon is  only a small taste of the game and I'm  curious to see what new enemies and  interesting levels can be built around  these new mechanics while doom eternal  doesn't have the shock of surprise the  previous doom had when people first  played it I'm glad to see the devs that  are pushing the follow-up game further  with new ideas hopefully it won't be too  long before we get a chance to play it  ourselves  [Music]

